{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NonPositiveDuration"],"anchor":"Simulations","title":"Simulations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime"],"anchor":"Time","title":"Time"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)"],"anchor":"States","title":"States"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation"},{"text":" owns a world and a set of schedules, each named by a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel"},{"text":". You add","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"systems to the schedules by label, then call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)"},{"text":" once a frame with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time that passed. The simulation decides which schedules run:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs once, before the first frame."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs once for every fixed timestep of time that has passed, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics and other rate-sensitive rules advance by the same amount each run, however uneven the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frames are."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/update","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" runs once a frame.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and systems:"}]},{"code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double }","struct FixedSteps: Resource { var count = 0 }","enum GameState: States { case menu, playing, paused }","","\/\/\/ Moves each entity by its velocity over one fixed timestep.","@System","struct Physics {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>, _ fixedTime: ResourceReader<FixedTime>) {","        let seconds = fixedTime.value.timestep \/ .seconds(1)","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx * seconds","        }","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Counts the runs of the schedule it is in.","@System","struct CountSteps {","    func run(_ steps: ResourceWriter<FixedSteps>) {","        steps.value.count += 1","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Spawns a ball at the origin.","@System","struct SpawnBall {","    func run(commands: inout Commands) {","        commands.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example runs ","type":"text"},{"code":"Physics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a fixed timestep of 1\/64 second, the default. A frame","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of 50 milliseconds covers three whole timesteps, so the ball moves three times:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","","var simulation = Simulation(world)","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics() }","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","","print(simulation.world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"States","anchor":"States","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A state type is a type, usually an enumeration, that conforms to "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": the screens of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game, or the phases of a simulation. Add one to a simulation with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". The simulation keeps the current state in the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resource; to change it, a system sets "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and the change applies at the start of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next frame. Entering, leaving and moving between states run schedules of their own,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onEnter(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onExit(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onTransition(from:to:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a run condition that holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in one state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example spawns a ball on entering the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"playing"},{"type":"text","text":" state and moves it only while the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game is in that state:"}]},{"code":["var simulation = Simulation()","simulation.add(state: GameState.menu)","simulation.add(to: .onEnter(GameState.playing)) { SpawnBall() }","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics().runIf(inState(GameState.playing)) }","","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"0\"","","simulation.world.resources[NextState<GameState>.self].set(.playing)","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.resources[CurrentState<GameState>.self].state)","\/\/ Prints \"playing\"","for (_, position) in simulation.world.query(Position.self) {","    print(position)  \/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"SimulationModule","externalID":"SimulationModule","modules":[{"name":"SimulationModule"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/simulationmodule"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/onEnter(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onEnter(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"onEnter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","text":"ScheduleLabel","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the label of the schedule that runs when a simulation enters the given state."}],"title":"onEnter(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/onenter(_:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/startup":{"abstract":[{"text":"The label of the schedule that runs once, before the first frame.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"startup"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","text":"ScheduleLabel"}],"title":"startup","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/startup"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/CurrentState":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CurrentState","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A resource holding the state a simulation is in.","type":"text"}],"title":"CurrentState","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/currentstate","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CurrentState","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/update":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The label of the schedule that runs once a frame."}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"update","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"update","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/update","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/update"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/add(state:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Adds a state type to the simulation, starting in the given state."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"add"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"state"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"add(state:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type